{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-091", "title": "Fix E2E test navigation selectors", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920261+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920268+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Critical  \n**Status**: Test selectors are incorrect  \n**Found In**: E2E automated testing\n\n## Problem\nThe E2E test script uses incorrect selectors for navigation links:\n- Test looks for: `a[href=\"#/\"]`\n- Actual structure: `<a href=\"/\" data-page=\"dashboard\">`\n\n## Impact\nNavigation tests fail with \"Navigation link not found\" for all 6 links.\n\n## Fix Required\nUpdate `e2e-test-script.js` line 64-69 to use correct selectors:\n```javascript\n{ selector: '[data-page=\"dashboard\"]', name: 'Dashboard' },\n{ selector: '[data-page=\"models\"]', name: 'Models' },\n{ selector: '[data-page=\"presets\"]', name: 'Presets' },\n{ selector: '[data-page=\"logs\"]', name: 'Logs' },\n{ selector: '[data-page=\"settings\"]', name: 'Settings' },\n```\n\n## Test Verification\nAfter fix, re-run: `node e2e-test-script.js` and verify navigation tests pass.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-7e8", "title": "Fix Chart.js tick generation warning", "status": "open", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920276+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920278+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Warning  \n**Status**: Performance warning in console  \n**Found In**: Dashboard page\n\n## Warning Message\n```\nscales.y.ticks.stepSize: 25 would result generating up to 1157629 ticks. Limiting to 1000.\n```\n\n## Root Cause\nChart configuration has stepSize: 25 which creates excessive tick requests for large data ranges.\n\n## Fix Required\nUpdate chart configuration in `public/js/components/dashboard/charts/chart-config.js`:\n\n```javascript\nscales: {\n  y: {\n    ticks: {\n      stepSize: 'auto',  // Let Chart.js optimize\n      maxTicksLimit: 100 // Hard limit\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Files Affected\n- `public/js/components/dashboard/charts/chart-config.js`\n\n## Test Verification\nAfter fix, reload dashboard and verify warning no longer appears in console.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-32a", "title": "Add Monitoring and Configuration to sidebar navigation", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920283+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920284+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Major  \n**Status**: Missing from sidebar navigation  \n**Found In**: User navigation\n\n## Problem\nTwo pages exist but are not accessible from the sidebar:\n1. **Monitoring** page - accessible via `/#/monitoring`\n2. **Configuration** page - accessible via `/#/configuration`\n\n## User Impact\nUsers cannot navigate to these pages from the main navigation.\n\n## Fix Required\nAdd links to sidebar in `public/js/components/layout/sidebar.js`:\n\n```javascript\n<a href=\"/monitoring\" class=\"nav-link\" data-page=\"monitoring\">\n  <span>\ud83d\udcc8</span><span>Monitoring</span>\n</a>\n<a href=\"/configuration\" class=\"nav-link\" data-page=\"configuration\">\n  <span>\ud83d\udd27</span><span>Configuration</span>\n</a>\n```\n\n## Files Affected\n- `public/js/components/layout/sidebar.js`\n\n## Alternative\nIf these pages are intentionally hidden, document why in `docs/README.md`.\n\n## Test Verification\nAfter fix, verify all 7 pages appear in sidebar navigation.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-54b", "title": "Verify ThresholdSettings component renders in Settings page", "status": "open", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "bug", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920288+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920290+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Major  \n**Status**: Threshold sliders not found  \n**Found In**: Settings page E2E test\n\n## Problem\nE2E test found 0 range sliders in Settings page, but ThresholdSettings component should provide threshold configuration sliders.\n\n## Expected Behavior\nSettings page should have 5 threshold sliders (CPU, Memory, GPU, Disk, Swap) with warning and alert levels.\n\n## Test Finding\n```\nTesting range sliders: Found 0 range sliders\n```\n\n## Verification Steps\n1. Navigate to Settings page\n2. Check if \"Alert Thresholds\" section appears\n3. Verify 5 metrics \u00d7 2 levels = 10 sliders are present\n\n## Files to Check\n- `public/js/pages/settings/components/threshold-settings.js`\n- `public/js/pages/settings/settings-page.js`\n\n## Test Verification\nAfter fix, re-run E2E test and verify 10+ range sliders found in Settings page.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-795", "title": "Add visible Socket.IO connection status indicator", "status": "open", "priority": 3, "issue_type": "enhancement", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920294+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920295+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Minor  \n**Status**: Status indicator not found in DOM  \n**Found In**: E2E test verification\n\n## Problem\nE2E test could not find connection status indicator element in the UI.\n\n## Current Behavior\n- Socket.IO connection is established (verified)\n- Visual indicator may exist but uses different class/structure\n\n## Expected Behavior\nUsers should see visual indicator of connection status (Connected/Disconnected).\n\n## Current Implementation\nSidebar has connection status but might not be visible or uses different classes.\n\n## Fix Options\n1. Make existing status indicator more visible\n2. Add status indicator to header\n3. Update test to find correct element\n\n## Files Affected\n- `public/js/components/layout/sidebar.js`\n\n## Test Verification\nAfter fix, verify connection status indicator is visible in sidebar.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
{"id": "nextjs-llama-async-proxy-e2e-ac5", "title": "Create comprehensive E2E test task list", "status": "open", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "test", "owner": "thebamer38@hotmail.com", "created_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920299+07:00", "created_by": "bamer", "updated_at": "2026-01-21T11:05:36.920301+07:00", "description": "**Severity**: Major  \n**Status**: Need systematic testing  \n**Found In**: E2E testing\n\n## Problem\nCurrent E2E tests are basic and don't cover all functionality.\n\n## Recommended Test Coverage\n\n### Navigation Tests\n- [ ] Test all sidebar links\n- [ ] Test browser back/forward buttons\n- [ ] Test direct URL navigation\n- [ ] Test 404 handling for invalid routes\n\n### Component Tests\n- [ ] Test all button clicks\n- [ ] Test all form inputs\n- [ ] Test all sliders\n- [ ] Test all modal triggers\n- [ ] Test all collapsible sections\n\n### State Tests\n- [ ] Test state updates after actions\n- [ ] Test Socket.IO event handling\n- [ ] Test notification display\n- [ ] Test loading states\n\n### Error Tests\n- [ ] Test error handling for failed requests\n- [ ] Test offline behavior\n- [ ] Test timeout handling\n- [ ] Test validation errors\n\n## Implementation\nCreate comprehensive test suite in `e2e-test-suite.js` with 100+ test cases.\n\n## Test Verification\nAll tests pass with 0 errors and 0 warnings.", "labels": ["e2e-test", "testing"]}
